<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kashtiliash IV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1232–1225 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century-bce">13th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kashtiliash IV was a Kassite king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> in the thirteenth century BCE. Around 1225 BCE he was defeated and captured by the Assyrian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tukulti-ninurta-i">Tukulti-Ninurta I</a>, who carried him in chains to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assur">Assur</a> and took control of Babylon, a victory celebrated in the Assyrian poem known as the Tukulti-Ninurta Epic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kashtiliash-iv.jpg" alt="Kashtiliash IV" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: V. Scheil · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tablet_of_Akapta%E1%B8%ABa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
